 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Everyone can draw, it's a learned skill, not talent. Spend ten minutes day practicing simple lines and basic shapes, soon you' see improvement. Start with simple drawings, like a box that turns when you fold it into a box, or a simple tree with three branches. A box that turns into a box has folds that make it flat, perfect for storing paper and pens. A tree with three branches is simple to draw. That's a good habit to break. Try drawing people doing different activities, like walking a dog or eating at a restaurant.",
